# Go build artifacts
/go/navlistener
/go/build/
/go/dist/
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# C feeder build artifact
/feeder/navfeeder

# GPL-quarantined bridge build artifact (out-of-process; never linked into the core)
/galmon-bridge/galmon-bridge

# Local config / secrets — config is TOML, never committed with real values
navlistener.toml
!navlistener.toml.example
*.local.toml

# TLS material / observer credentials — never commit
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# Claude local machine settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Reference ICDs (reference/icd/, catalogued in reference/REFERENCES.md):
# redistribution-permitted documents are vendored explicitly (negated below);
# all others remain local-only until their licenses are cleared. Terms per
# document are recorded in REFERENCES.md; add a negation line when a doc's
# reproduction grant is confirmed from the document itself.
reference/icd/*.pdf
# US Government works — public domain (Distribution Statement A / no © asserted):
!reference/icd/IS-GPS-200N.pdf
!reference/icd/IS-GPS-705J.pdf
!reference/icd/IS-GPS-800J.pdf
!reference/icd/ICD-GPS-240D.pdf
!reference/icd/WAAS-PS.pdf
# EU — conditional "© European Union" reproduction grant printed in the document
# (redistribution permitted with the Terms of Use carried unmodified alongside):
!reference/icd/GAL-OS-SIS-ICD-2.2.pdf
!reference/icd/GAL-OSNMA-SIS-ICD.pdf
!reference/icd/GAL-OSNMA-RXG.pdf
!reference/icd/GAL-HAS-SIS-ICD.pdf
!reference/icd/EGNOS-SDD-OS.pdf
# Japan CAO — explicit redistribution clause in the document's Additional Terms of Use:
!reference/icd/QZSS-DCR.pdf
# IGS/RTCM open format standards — published openly at files.igs.org, no © asserted:
!reference/icd/RINEX-3.05.pdf
!reference/icd/RINEX-4.02.pdf
!reference/icd/SP3-D.pdf
# NOTE: all other reference/icd/*.pdf (BeiDou, GLONASS, QZSS-PNT/L1S/L6, NavIC) stay
# local-only — their terms grant no redistribution (or NavIC-L5S forbids it). NavIC-L1
# carries only a conditional non-profit grant and is held local-only by decision.
# See reference/REFERENCES.md for per-document terms.
